commit 1aad1d4403d9521ac8b2dfb6b015cb9f086345fe
Author: missingbulb <73882448+missingbulb@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Fri Sep 25 20:35:32 2026 +0300

    PlanNG: a faded photograph of the host city behind the top of the page (#897)

    When a festival leads the trip, a faint photograph of its city sits behind
    the year strip and the page title, cross-fading with the genre colours when
    another festival takes the lead (an instant switch under reduced motion).
    The year card is translucent so the city shows through it, and the footer
    credits the photograph with its source and licence.

    Photos of Jerusalem, Haifa, Akko and Edinburgh are from Wikimedia Commons
    (CC0, CC BY-SA 4.0, CC BY 2.0, CC BY 2.0), scaled to 1600px WebP and
    stored under site/planNG/cities/.

    Spec 23.17-23.19, with the planNG goldens the photo, the translucent card
    and the extra footer line move refreshed.


    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0123Qx6CPBFuPk1bG7rfFzZo

    Co-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>

